      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This article reviews the more common causes of abdominal pain in children. It is divided into three sections to emphasize differential diagnosis. For some problems responsible for abdominal pain surgery is essential, for some surgery may not be initially required but may be unavoidable, and for others the condition is purely medical and surgery should be avoided. Armed with a complete differential diagnosis, the general surgical resident may avoid many pitfalls."},
